     "Ann Wolbert Burgess (born 1936) made her name studying rape victims in 1970s Boston and helped define rape trauma. The FBI brought her in to help code the prison interviews into a research database, and she co-wrote Sexual Homicide (1988) with Ressler and Douglas, and the Crime Classification Manual. She once arrived to interview victims of a serial rapist and local police phoned the FBI to check, assuming a woman claiming to work with the Bureau was an impostor. The Mindhunter character Wendy Carr is loosely based on her, and Hulu's 2024 documentary Mastermind: To Think Like a Killer tells her story.",
