     "Edmund Kemper killed his grandparents at 15, was released in 1969, and between May 1972 and April 1973 murdered seven women, including his mother, and one girl. Most of his victims were hitchhiking students near Santa Cruz; he had a university parking sticker from his mother's job, so women trusted his car. Tested in custody, he scored an IQ of 136. Kemper became one of the FBI's most forthcoming interviewees, and Mindhunter cast him as the agents' first teacher. That is the catch: a profile built from killers who enjoy talking may describe talkers, not killers.",
